<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 17 April, from 1492 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1492 CE <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus and the Spanish Crown agree the Capitulations of Santa Fe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ferdinand and Isabella agreed terms with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> for a westward voyage, promising him the title of admiral and a tenth of the wealth from any lands he found.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1521 CE <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luther is summoned to recant before the Diet of Worms</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Before Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> acknowledged his books but asked for time to answer whether he would retract them. The next day he refused, defying both emperor and Pope.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1895 CE <span class="tih-ago">131 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Shimonoseki ends the First Sino-Japanese War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> recognised Korean independence, ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penghu">Pescadores</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and paid a large indemnity. Defeat exposed the weakness of the Qing and announced Japan as a regional power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war">First Sino-Japanese War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1946 CE <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Last French troops leave Syria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The withdrawal of the final French forces completed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>'s independence after a quarter-century of mandate rule. The day is still marked in Syria as Evacuation Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1961 CE <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cuban exiles land at the Bay of Pigs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A CIA-trained brigade of some 1,400 Cuban exiles landed in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> to overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>. They were defeated within three days, a grave embarrassment for the new Kennedy administration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1975 CE <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Khmer Rouge take Phnom Penh</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> forces entered the Cambodian capital and immediately drove its population into the countryside. Their rule until 1979 led to the deaths of an estimated 1.5 to 2 million people.</p></div></li></ol>
